\begin{eqnarray*}
Tv(k_{1}) & = & {\displaystyle \max_{k_{1}^{\prime}}}\ u(f(k_{1})-k_{1}^{\prime})+\beta v(k_{2}^{\prime})\\
 & = & u(f(k_{1})-h(k_{1}))+\beta v(h(k_{1}))\\
Tv(k_{2}) & = & {\displaystyle \max_{k_{2}^{\prime}}}\ u(f(k_{2})-k_{2}^{\prime})+\beta v(k_{2}^{\prime})\\
 & = & u(f(k_{2})-h(k_{2}))+\beta v(h(k_{2}))
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $f(k)\equiv F(k,1)+(1-\delta)k$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $F(k,1)$
\end_inset

 is strictly concave and strictly increasing, then so is 
\begin_inset Formula $f(k)$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset Formula $h(\cdot)$
\end_inset

 is the optimal solution of the maximization problem.
 So, we have found the policy function 
\begin_inset Formula $h(\cdot)$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $h(k_{1})=k_{1}^{\prime}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $h(k_{2})=k_{2}^{\prime}$
\end_inset

.
