\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

To end this section, we provide some economic intuition concerning the results
 that have just been derived.
 From the Euler equation, we have
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
u^{\prime}(c_{t})=\beta\left[\frac{\partial F(k,1)}{\partial k}+1-\delta\right]u^{\prime}(c_{t+1})
\]

\end_inset

If 
\begin_inset Formula $c_{t+1}>c_{t}$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $u^{\prime}(c_{t})>u^{\prime}(c_{t+1})$
\end_inset

, so
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
\beta\left[\frac{\partial F(k,1)}{\partial k}+1-\delta\right]>1\\
\frac{\partial F(k,1)}{\partial k}=\frac{1}{\beta}-(1-\delta)>0
\end{gather*}

\end_inset

In addition, we can conclude that
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
h(k)<k^{*}\iff h(k)>k\implies\mbox{the economy is growing}\\
h(k)>k^{*}\iff h(k)<k\implies\mbox{the economy is shrinking}\\
h(k)=k\iff h(k^{*})=k^{*}\implies\mbox{the economy stays the same}
\end{gather*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

